;; Trusted disposable evidence-review profile; descriptions only.
{"bash" "Trusted evidence-review profile: bash permits only the exact command true, a no-op. Do not use bash for file inspection, directory listing, grep, match counts, redirects, or any other shell command. Use glob for filename discovery, directory-scoped grep for bounded search, and read for known files. The existing permissions remain authoritative."
 "grep" "Trusted evidence-review profile: use grep only for bounded discovery with path set to a known existing directory and include set to a narrow filename glob. A file-valued path may search its containing directory. To inspect an exact file, especially a large diff, JSON, or generated source map, use read instead. Search output can be clipped and is not complete file evidence. Do not redirect match counts or other work to bash."
 "read" "Trusted evidence-review profile: read a known existing file path, discovered with glob when needed, starting at offset 1. Follow the returned continuation with explicit offsets until EOF. Retain every page and treat clipped or incomplete content as incomplete evidence; do not infer omitted bytes. Do not guess a missing file or use bash as a workaround. A failed host tool call remains subject to the existing strict invocation and recovery policy."
 "glob" "Trusted evidence-review profile: use glob for bounded filename discovery in a known directory before reading an uncertain path or manifest. Returned filenames establish discovery only; inspect known files with read and follow its continuation to EOF. Use directory-scoped grep with an explicit include for bounded content discovery. Do not use bash for discovery."}
